# CODEOWNERS — review-routing ownership map for the Dubiz repository.
#
# Context (2026-07-31): the repository currently has a SINGLE maintainer
# (@eldad8802-prog — the only account with write/admin access). Every rule
# below therefore resolves to that one owner. The per-path structure is
# intentional: it documents the security-sensitive surfaces and is ready for a
# dedicated security reviewer / second maintainer to be added later without a
# restructure.
#
# NOTE: this file only routes review *requests*. It becomes enforcing only if
# branch protection is set to "require review from Code Owners" — which is
# deliberately NOT enabled at this stage (single-maintainer self-merge policy).
# Syntax: last matching pattern wins.

# ── Default owner ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*                                   @eldad8802-prog

# ── Authentication & session ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
/lib/auth.ts                        @eldad8802-prog
/lib/auth-token.ts                  @eldad8802-prog
/lib/auth/                          @eldad8802-prog
/app/api/auth/                      @eldad8802-prog

# ── Security primitives (rate limiting; perimeter gateway) ───────────────────
/lib/security/                      @eldad8802-prog
/middleware.ts                      @eldad8802-prog          # perimeter gateway (T13; file not yet created — forward-declared)

# ── Tenant model, schema & migrations ───────────────────────────────────────
/prisma/                            @eldad8802-prog

# ── Storage & file handling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
/lib/storage/                       @eldad8802-prog

# ── Integration credentials & cryptography ──────────────────────────────────
/lib/services/integrations/         @eldad8802-prog
/lib/services/payments/             @eldad8802-prog
/lib/services/billing/authority/    @eldad8802-prog

# ── Platform admin ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/app/api/platform-admin/            @eldad8802-prog
/lib/auth/platform-admin.ts         @eldad8802-prog

# ── Repository & CI/CD configuration ────────────────────────────────────────
/.github/                           @eldad8802-prog

# ── Security governance & strategy documents ────────────────────────────────
/docs/security-*                    @eldad8802-prog

# ── Release & deployment infrastructure (see docs/RELEASE-OWNERSHIP.md) ─────
/vercel.json                        @eldad8802-prog
/.vercelignore                      @eldad8802-prog
/scripts/ci/release-*               @eldad8802-prog
/scripts/ci/migration-first-guard.mjs  @eldad8802-prog
/docs/RELEASE-OWNERSHIP.md          @eldad8802-prog

# ── Security proof system & delivery pipeline (sec/A, 2026-09-24) ───────────
# Every path whose edit can change what CI proves, what reaches Production, or
# who a tenant is. Listed explicitly (not only via the defaults above) so the
# map survives a future narrowing of `*` and so a second reviewer / review App
# added later is routed here first. Enforcing ONLY once branch protection sets
# "require review from Code Owners" with a reviewer other than the PR author —
# see docs/security/ci-owner-actions.md.
/.github/**                         @eldad8802-prog
/prisma/migrations/**               @eldad8802-prog
/scripts/ci/**                      @eldad8802-prog
/lib/tenant/**                      @eldad8802-prog
/lib/auth.ts                        @eldad8802-prog
/lib/auth*/**                       @eldad8802-prog
/lib/auth-token.ts                  @eldad8802-prog
/lib/prisma*.ts                     @eldad8802-prog
/lib/services/account/**            @eldad8802-prog
/lib/services/payments/**           @eldad8802-prog
/proxy.ts                           @eldad8802-prog
